<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Maroboduus</h1><p class="st-meta">9 BCE – 19 CE (approx.) · capital Marobudum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first large Germanic kingdom known by name, built in Bohemia by Maroboduus, who drilled an army on Roman lines and alarmed Augustus.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroboduus">Maroboduus</a>, a Marcomannic noble who had spent his youth in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, led his people from the Main region into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> around 9 BCE to escape Roman offensives. There he subjected neighbouring peoples, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/quadi">Quadi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lugii">Lugii</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semnones">Semnones</a> and Langobardi, building a realm that stretched from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> and beyond.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velleius-paterculus">Velleius Paterculus</a> describes a centralised monarchy with a standing army of about 70,000 foot and 4,000 horse trained in Roman fashion; its royal seat may be the Marobudum named by Ptolemy. Roman merchants lived there. Augustus planned to crush him in 6 CE with twelve legions, but the Pannonian revolt forced a treaty recognising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroboduus">Maroboduus</a> as a friend of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroboduus">Maroboduus</a> stayed neutral when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-quinctilius-varus">Varus</a>' legions in 9, and in 17 Arminius defeated him; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semnones">Semnones</a> and Langobardi deserted. In 19 the Gothic exile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catualda">Catualda</a> seized his capital, and Maroboduus fled to Roman territory, dying in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ravenna">Ravenna</a> in 37. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> then created the client <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vannius">Kingdom of Vannius</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 9 BCE – 19 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:59.52%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>9 BCE – 19 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Marobudum</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maroboduus, Catualda</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Germanic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Elbe Germanic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, <a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marcomannic Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=5&amp;focus=kingdom-of-maroboduus" aria-label="Kingdom of Maroboduus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5029 445 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Maroboduus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5349 701h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5349 701h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Czech Republic. <a href="/atlas?year=5&amp;focus=kingdom